          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em pointed topological space
            (often
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+space"} pointed space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            equipped with a choice of one of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points"} points
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"}> elements
            ). If the inclusion of that point is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+cofibration"} Hurewicz cofibration
            then one speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topological+space"} well-pointed topological space
          %p
            Although this concept may seem simple, pointed topological spaces play a central role for instance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            as domains for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"} reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theories"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theories
            and as an ingredient for the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %p
            One reason why pointed topological spaces are important is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            which they form is an intermediate stage in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical homotopy theory of topological spaces
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %p
            The category of pointed topological spaces has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
            itself) and the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            on pointed spaces is the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product of topological space
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em pointed topological space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
            equipped with a choice of point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            between pointed topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,y)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            which preserves the chosen basepoints in that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
          %h3#the_category_of_pointed_topological_spaces The category of pointed topological spaces
          %p
            Stated in the language of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of topological spaces. This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
            of topological spaces “under” the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
          %p
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon \ast  \to (X,\tau)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            (hence a continuous function), such that this triangle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commutes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi x
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{x}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{y}}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\\
                  X &amp;&amp; \underset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; Y
                  }
          %p
            which equivalently means that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
          %h3#ForgettingAndAdjoiningBasepoints Forgetting and adjoining basepoints
          #BasePointAdjoined.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/} \to Top
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              given by forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
              (“adjoining a base point”), this is denoted by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)_+ \coloneqq (-) \sqcup \ast \;\colon \; Top \longrightarrow Top^{\ast/}
                    \\,.
          %h3#wedge_sum_and_smash_product Wedge sum and Smash product
          #WedgeSumAsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Given two pointed topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,y)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
                  is simply their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
                  equipped with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  of basepoints
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X\times Y, (x,y))
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
                  has to be computed using the second clause in
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a{:href => "pointed+object#LimitsAndColimitsOfPointedObjects"} this prop.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                  has to be adjoined to the diagram, it is given not by the coproduct in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                  (which is the
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                  of the form:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi x
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-50%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mrow
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mrow
                                          %mrow
                                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                            %mi po
                                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                                %mo ∨
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\ast &amp;\overset{x}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{y}}\downarrow
                        \&amp;\mathclap{{}^{{}_{(po)}}}&amp;
                        \\downarrow
                        \\\
                        Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \vee Y
                        }
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This is called the
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  operation on pointed objects.
                %p
                  This is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+space"} quotient topological space
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
                  under the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
                  which identifies the two basepoints:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X \vee Y \;\simeq\; (X \sqcup Y)/(x \sim y)
            %p
              Generally for a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(X_i,x_i)\}_{i \in I}
              of pointed topological spaces
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  is formed in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                  with the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+topology"} Tychonoff topology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_i)_{i \in I} \in \underset{i \in I}{\prod} X_i
                  of basepoints being the new basepoint;
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  is formed by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                  over the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  with a basepoint adjoined, and is called the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∨
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_{i \in I} X_i
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+space"} quotient topological space
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
                  with all the basepoints identified:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∨
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∼
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{i \in I}{\vee} X_i
                        \\;\simeq\;
                        \\left(\underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} X_i\right)/(x_i \sim x_j)_{i,j \in I}
                        \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of its
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
              = succeed "-spheres," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo ∨
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^n / X^{n-1} \simeq \underset{i \in I_n}{\vee} S^n
                    \\,.
          #SmashProductOfPointedObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of pointed topological spaces is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)\wedge(-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Top^{\ast/}
                    \\times
                    Top^{\ast/}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Top^{\ast/}
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \wedge Y
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\ast
                    \\underset{X\sqcup Y}{\sqcup} (X \times Y)
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \sqcup Y &amp;\overset{(id_X,y),(x,id_Y) }{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \times Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \wedge Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              from def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              (
              %a{:href => "quotient+space#QuotientBySubspace"}> this def
              ) of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              constituted by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ≃
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \wedge Y \simeq \frac{X\times Y}{X \vee Y}
                    \\,.
          %p
            t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th symbol
                %th name
                %th category theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \vee Y
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi Y
                        %mo =
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∨
                            %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \wedge Y = \frac{X \times Y}{X \vee Y}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
          #WedgeAndSmashOfBasePointAdjoinedTopologicalSpaces.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in Top
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo +
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mo +
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+,Y_+ \in Top^{\ast/}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasePointAdjoined"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                        %mo ∨
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo +
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi Y
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+ \vee Y_+ \simeq (X \sqcup Y)_+
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo +
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+ \wedge Y_+ \simeq (X \times Y)_+
                  \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+ \vee Y_+
              is given by the colimit in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              over the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\,\,&amp; \ast &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \ast &amp;\,\,&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is clearly
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo *
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \sqcup \ast \sqcup B
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductOfPointedObjects"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo +
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mo +
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∨
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Y
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Y
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mi Y
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mi Y
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mo *
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    X_+ \wedge Y_+
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\frac{(X \sqcup \ast) \times (X \sqcup \ast)}{(X\sqcup \ast) \vee (Y \sqcup \ast)}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\frac{X \times Y \sqcup X \sqcup Y \sqcup \ast}{X \sqcup Y \sqcup \ast}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    X \times Y \sqcup \ast
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          #StandardReducedCyclinderInTop.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq [0,1] \subset \mathbb{R}
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_+ \in Top^{\ast/}
            %p
              is the interval with a disjoint basepoint adjoined, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasePointAdjoined"}
            %p
              Now for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductOfPointedObjects"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \wedge (I_+) = (X \times I)/(\{x_0\} \times I)
            %p
              is the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cylinder"} reduced cylinder
              over
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the point.
            %p
              (Generally, any construction in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              properly adapted to pointed spaces is called the “reduced” version of the unpointed construction. Notably so for “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"}> reduced suspension
              ” which we come to
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "#MappingCones"} below
            %p
              Just like the ordinary cylinder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times I
              receives a canonical injection from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sqcup X
              formed in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sqcup X
              formed in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              from example
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \vee X \longrightarrow X \wedge (I_+)
                    \\,.
          %h3#mapping_cocones Mapping (co-)cones
          %p
            Recall that the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
            with the closed interval
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Cone(X)
                  \=
                  (X \times [0,1])/( X \times \{0\} )
                  \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is pointed with basepoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %em reduced cone
            is the further quotient by the copy of the interval over the basepoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Cone(X,x) = Cone(X) / ( \{x\} \times [0,1] )
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/attachment+space"} attachment space
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cyl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi f
                      %mi Cyl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Cyl(f) \coloneqq Y \cup_f Cyl(X)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/attachment+space"} attachment space
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi f
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Cone(f) \coloneqq Y \cup_f Cone(X)
          %p
            accordingly if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            is a continuous function between pointed spaces which preserves the basepoint, then the analogous construction with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cylinder"} reduced cylinder
            and the reduce cone, respectively, yield the
            %em reduced mapping cyclinder
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %em reduced mapping cone
          %p
            We now say this again in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
          #MappingConeAndMappingCocone.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              between pointed spces, its
              %strong
                reduced
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              is the space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo *
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi X
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi X
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cone(f)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\ast \underset{X}{\sqcup} Cyl(X) \underset{X}{\sqcup} Y
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimiting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
